Current original Zero workflow (0.12)

Use the native tools on Linux or their .exe versions on Windows:
  zero-integrate PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_KERNEL.zero
  zero-build PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY NEW_KERNEL.zero
  zero-check PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_TEST_DIRECTORY
All destination paths must be new. The integrator preserves authored sources;
the builder checks its compiler fixed point and builds the original targets;
the verifier checks language behavior and host file operations in process.
See tools/integrate.ztext, tools/build.ztext and checks/README.ztext.
Read these documents with zero-text read FILE.

The notes below preserve earlier implementation and test history. Any old
shell/Python runner names, generated artifacts, JSON reports or commands are
historical references: they were removed from the active project and are not
current runnable instructions or current-release validation. Native host
checks do not replace BIOS/UEFI, persistence or physical-hardware testing.

Historical implementation notes

Original Zero native-tool boot verification

Run from project root: python3 review-tests/guest-bundle/run.py
Host Python only orchestrates builds, firmware VMs and independent byte checks.
All boot code, native applications, container writers and guest probes are Zero.
The default compiler is build/zero; ZERO_TEST_COMPILER may override it.
App fixtures come from build/guest-app/{zero,frontend,pack}{64,32}.app; parent
integration rebuilds those targets from the final merged compiler separately.

Validates the 480 KiB kernel layout, 1 MiB native compiler bundle, complete FAT
chains and ISO extents/catalog/endian fields, exact payload equality, malformed
app headers/padding, writer failures, four actual firmware/CPU paths and BIOS
low-RAM refusal. The guest probe computes a weighted checksum of all 1 MiB of
the loaded bundle, checks kernel markers through byte491519, and writes/reads
both ends of every 4 KiB page in the 8 MiB workspace. It also validates kernel
pool bounds and that the bundle/workspace/pool do not overlap.

The runner writes only private build/guest-bundle.* and evidence files. It
never attaches a writable data disk, asserts existing data.img/data.vdi/live
ISO hashes unchanged and stops all its VMs. Evidence is recorded in
verification/guest-bundle-480k-runtime64k/. Historical28KiB runtime-slot
evidence remains in verification/guest-bundle-480k/. Actual native compiler pipeline execution is
covered separately by portability/guest tests and verification/guest-app/.
Native VirtualBox and physical hardware are not claimed by QEMU tests.

Runtime storage expansion (0.10)
python3 review-tests/guest-bundle/runtime-capacity.py runs component checks only.
It covers the actual host-files runtime,65,535-byte maximum body, strict zero
padding, invalid/oversized/short inputs, input/output errors and fragmented
reads. It builds only the original Zero bundle writer, leaves the live ISO
and data disks untouched and starts no VM. Its separate evidence is in
verification/guest-bundle-runtime64k/. The expanded runtime slot does not
change app offsets, the1MiB bundle, boot loader allocations or ISO geometry.
